RISC3D 0.10 for RISC OS on Linux (prototype)
============================================

What it puts where:
  /opt/riscos/rol-3d                        Linux's side: draws for RISC OS
                                            programs with Linux's Mesa (the
                                            GPU's driver: v3d on a Pi 4/5)
  HardDisc4.!Boot.Resources.!RISC3D         RISC3D, as on native RISC OS:
    .RISC3D                                 the RISC3D module (driver interface)
    .GPU.Linux3D                            its driver for RISC OS on Linux
                                            (RISC3D loads it itself)
  HardDisc4.!Boot.Choices.Boot.PreDesk.RISC3D   loads RISC3D at start-up
                                            (made once; yours to delete)

Programs need nothing in their !Run: !RISC3D's !Boot loads RISC3D.

init (riscos-support 1.0.0049-1 or later) starts rol-3d at start-up; with
an earlier one, this package starts it when installed, and it has to be
started again after each restart (as root: setsid /opt/riscos/rol-3d &).
Its log: /riscos/3d/log.txt.

Programs use it through riscos-mesa's EGL (from riscos-mesa's release with
RISC3D). Set RISC3D$Disable to turn it off for programs started after.

Zero-copy frames (straight onto the screen) need rol-fb's overlays
(riscos-support 1.0.0048-1 or later) and a 16 million colour mode.

The SWI chunk (&C3D00) and error numbers (&81D3xx) are provisional.
